1
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:06,240
亲爱的 你会买一款叫做...
Honey, would you buy a closet called --

2
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:09,520
我在等通知 看我明天能不能去
I am waiting to see if I get to go tomorrow.

3
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,460
陪审员义务 其实你可以直接把电话扔在一边
Jury duty. You know, you can just throw that away.

4
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:13,340
那样他们就无法通知你你被选中了
There's no way they can ever tell you got it.

5
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,600
杰 你是不合格的美国人
Jay, you're a bad American.

6
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,460
能在陪审团发挥作用是一种荣耀
It is a privilege to serve on a jury.

7
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,480
我有史以来第一次可以参与了
For the first time, I get to be part of it.

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,500
等你吃着从自动售货机买来的
Talk to me when you're eating

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,860
金枪鱼三明治再跟我说这话吧
a tuna sandwich out of a machine.

10
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:26,220
总之 那款是浮雕橡木材质 我想取名为...
Anyway, it's a distressed-oak model that I like to call --

11
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:27,480
等等 等等 等着
Wait, wait! Wait!

12
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:29,500
我被选中了
I'm in!

13
00:00:29,676 --> 00:00:32,920
明早8点 C区停车楼
8:00 a.m. tomorrow. Parking structure "C"!

14
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,280
你对停车楼感到很激动吗
You're excited about a parking structure?

15
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,720
连A区或B区都不是
It's not even "A" or "B."

16
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,860
你得接替我去乔的学校做伴护
You're gonna have to take my place working at Joe's school.

17
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,280
我做不到啊 我有工作的
I can't do that. I have a job.

18
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:41,680
让克莱尔帮你顶着
Have Claire cover for you.

19
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:44,120
她知道怎么吼员工 看报纸
She knows how to yell at people and read the newspaper.

20
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,820
那学校是有什么毛病啊
What the hell's wrong with that school?

21
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,160
我们付他们钱 不就是为了不用亲自照顾孩子吗
Aren't we paying them so we don't have to take care of our kid?

22
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:50,420
学习谷仓不是这种制度
That's not the way it works at the learning barn.

23
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:53,360
他们希望家长也能参与进来
You know that they want the parents to be involved

24
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,760
那样就能增进跟孩子的感情
so that they can bond with the kids.

25
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,200
这年头的学校是发什么神经啊
What's wrong with schools today?

26
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,180
我现在很成功
I'm successful,

27
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:58,880
我当年的老师不过就是个长胡子的修女
and I had a nun with a mustache.

28
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,320
你最好习惯到那里去
Well, you better get used to going there,

29
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,600
因为如果我参审[卷入]的是件谋杀案
Because if I get put into a murder trial,

30
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,440
我可能得去[进牢]好几周呢
I could be gone for weeks.

31
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:05,900
或许我该告诉他们
Maybe I should tell them

32
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,040
我有在枪决队的经验
that I have experience on a firing squad.

33
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,760
你为什么要说这种疯话啊
Why do you say crazy stuff like that?

34
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,340
那不是真的 对吧
Now, that isn't true, is it?

35
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:12,440
等等
Wait a second.

36
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,640
那款新衣柜 我刚刚说叫什么来着
That new closet, what did I say it was called?

37
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:15,880
你没说出来
You never said.

38
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:16,700
该死的
Damn it!

39
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,240
我洗澡时非得要放支油性铅笔在旁边
That's why I need a grease pencil in the shower.

40
00:01:32,907 --> 00:01:33,994
我也说不清 海莉
Oh, I don't know, Haley.

41
00:01:33,994 --> 00:01:38,160
他很帅 很聪明 也很幽默
I mean, he is really cute and really smart and really funny,

42
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:41,160
但是 他总是穿木底鞋
But, oh, he's always wearing clogs.

43
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:42,840
不 不行
No, no.

44
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,100
如果他不是个大厨 护士或是郁金香销售员
If he is not a chef, a nurse, or a tulip salesman,

45
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,040
你得赶紧躲开
you need to run.

46
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:49,480
如果你妈对穿木底鞋的男人也是这种态度
If your mother had that attitude about a man in clogs,

47
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,920
你们俩就不会有我这亲爹了
you two wouldn't have a dad.

48
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:53,160
好的 谢谢 老爸 我不会让你失望的
Okay, thanks, Dad. I won't let you down.

49
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:53,780
再见
Bye.

50
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,700
猜猜怎么着 各位
Guess what, guys.

51
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:58,020
明天我会暂时充当公司的老大
I am going to be the big boss at work tomorrow,

52
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:00,720
巧的是 明天恰好是"带女儿去公司日"
And coincidentally, it's take your daughter to work day.

53
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,400
我可以跟你一起去公司 老妈
I'll go to work with you, Mom.

54
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,180
别想逃避社区服务了
Stop trying to get out of community service.

55
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,640
你需要攒够足够时间才能毕业
You need those hours to graduate.

56
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:06,900
再说你又不是女儿身
And you're not a daughter.

57
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,100
老妈 老爸 坐下
Mom, Dad, sit down.

58
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:10,760
我有件事要告诉你们
There's something I need to talk to you about.

59
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:11,340
你必须去
You're going.

60
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,260
姑娘们 你们意下如何
So, girls, what do you say?

61
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,760
我们又不是八岁小孩了 我还是有工作的人
You know we're not 8, and I have a job.

62
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,300
你上周因为长了青春痘 就请了两次病假
You called in sick twice last week because you had a zit.

63
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,120
我是在时尚行业工作的 他们叫我别去的
I work in fashion. They told me not to come in.

64
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,180
艾丽克斯 宝贝
Alex, honey,

65
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,174
你明天最后一节课是上午10点
your last class tomorrow is at 10:00 a.m.,

66
00:02:24,174 --> 00:02:24,720
-不 不 不 -如果你早点出发
- No, no, no, no! -So, if you hit the road

67
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:25,740
海莉 快把电脑合上
Haley, quick, close the laptop!

68
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:28,320
在此之前 我一直是个全职妈妈
Until now, I was always a full-time mom,

69
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:31,300
所以女儿们一直没能看到我的另一面
So the girls never had a chance to see the other side of me --

70
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,700
就是 强势的女高层
You know, powerful woman in charge.

71
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:36,068
是啊 我们从"没机会"看到你强势的一面呢
Yeah, 'cause we never get to see your tough side.

72
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,980
快点 大爸 你工作要迟到了
Come on, Daddy, we're gonna be late for your work.

73
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,220
我知道 我也很激动
I know. I'm excited, too.

74
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:45,860
好吧 我错了
Okay, I was wrong.

75
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:47,040
在外吹口哨并没有好一些
The whistles aren't better outside.

76
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,140
你确定你一个人可以把这些杂货都弄回家吗
Are you sure you can get all these groceries home by yourself?

77
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,480
我不知道 我有点害怕
I don't know. I'm kind of scared.

78
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,080
我以前从未开车载过杂货回家呢
I've never driven groceries home before.

79
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:54,040
你们好啊
Hey, you guys.

80
00:02:54,879 --> 00:02:56,247
雷 雷蒙德
Ray-- Raymond?

81
00:02:56,247 --> 00:02:58,360
你好啊 好久不见
Hi. Oh, it's been so long.

82
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:01,220
是啊 自从那事后 就没见过你们了
Yeah. Haven't seen you since, you know.

83
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:02,400
是啊
Yeah.

84
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:05,300
雷蒙德和杰马库斯三个月前分手了
Raymond and J'marcus broke up three months ago,

85
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,600
他们在一起的时间和我们差不多
And they'd been together almost as long as we have.

86
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,000
杰马库斯继续和原来的朋友交往着
J'marcus got all the friends,

87
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,840
而雷蒙德沦落到穿着睡衣去购物
And Raymond got all the confidence to go shopping in his pajamas.

88
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:13,940
你们要办派对吗
You guys having a party?

89
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,960
-不 什么派对 -不 不是办派对
- No, no. Party? - No, not a party.

90
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:20,149
橄榄杂烩 方巾 三式饼干
Olive medley, square napkins, cracker trio.

91
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,360
这些东西只是为了...
well, these things are just more for a --

92
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,200
你觉得该怎么说好呢
What would you say?

93
00:03:23,289 --> 00:03:23,960
小聚吗
Kind of like a get-together?

94
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,480
小聚 小聚 是临时决定的
Get-together, get-together. It's a last-minute thing.

95
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,340
没什么的
It's no big deal.

96
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,220
听上去很有趣
Sounds fun.

97
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,020
-不 很无趣的 -是啊 就饼干嘛
- No, it's not gonna be fun. - No. It's crackers.

98
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:30,940
到时候会下雨的
It's supposed to rain.

99
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:32,980
那再见了
I'll see you guys.

100
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:34,560
-好 -回见了 雷蒙德
- Yes. - You, too, Raymond.

101
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:36,219
-再见 -照顾好自己
- Bye-bye. - Take care of yourself.

102
00:03:38,019 --> 00:03:38,622
刚刚好险啊
That was close.

103
00:03:38,622 --> 00:03:39,980
我以为我们不得不邀请他了呢
I thought we were gonna have to invite him.

104
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,320
雷蒙德 你今晚也该来的
Raymond, you should come tonight.

105
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:42,780
真的吗
Really?

106
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:45,200
没有雷蒙德 算什么小聚啊
It wouldn't be a get-together without Raymond.

107
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,720
-对吧 小卡 -绝对的
- Right, Cam? - Absolutely.

108
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,340
是啊 但是你知道吗 那个...
Yeah. Oh, you know what? But...

109
00:03:49,223 --> 00:03:51,873
我得提醒你一下 杰马库斯也会去的
I should tell you, J'marcus is gonna be there.

110
00:03:51,884 --> 00:03:53,780
所以如果你觉得那样很尴尬
So, if that's gonna be uncomfortable,

111
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,940
我们完全理解的
we totally understand.

112
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,375
不 没事 我会去的
No, it's fine. I'll be there.

113
00:03:57,375 --> 00:03:59,164
能再次见到杰马库斯也挺好的
It'll be nice to see J'marcus again.

114
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:02,160
或许他会带一个裸上身的腹肌婊过去
Maybe he'll bring one of those shirtless ab sluts

115
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,600
我在他脸书上都看到了
I've seen on his facebook page.

116
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,320
-回见 -好的 回见
- I'll see you guys. - Yeah. Yeah, see ya.

117
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,093
好的 我很期待
Okay. Look forward to it.

118
00:04:07,093 --> 00:04:07,927
-回见 -好的
- you, too. - Yeah.

119
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,780
我能怎么做啊
What was I supposed to do?

120
00:04:10,893 --> 00:04:13,980
他那么伤心 可悲 心碎
I mean, he was all sad and pathetic and broken.

121
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:16,580
是啊 任何派对都需要这样一个人呢
Well, yes, the perfect addition to any party.

122
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,340
他们一定会撕逼撕得天昏地暗
They are gonna be at each other's throats

123
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:19,860
毁了整个晚上 走吧 莉莉
and ruin the whole night. Come on, Lily.

124
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:20,940
都怪你 这次的派对
Thanks to you, we are throwing

125
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:22,320
肯定是这个社交季最反社会的
the antisocial event of the season.

126
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,360
-小卡 -不 先不说了 我要迟到了
- Cam. - No, I'm late and I'd like to leave on that.

127
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:31,060
你好 我来了
Hi. I'm -- I'm here.

128
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:33,560
真是惊喜啊
Well, this is a special treat.

129
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:37,837
我竟然看到了一位第一次出现的志愿者
I spy with my little eye a first-time volunteer!

130
00:04:37,837 --> 00:04:39,000
歌洛莉亚要去做陪审团
Gloria had jury duty,

131
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,740
所以我能假装种族歧视
so no chance I could get out of this

132
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,980
不来做志愿者吗
by pretending to be racist?

133
00:04:42,409 --> 00:04:44,650
总之 你要我做什么
Anyway, uh... what do you need?

134
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:48,440
你可以准备颜料 做甘蓝冰沙
You can set up the paints, make the kale smoothies,

135
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,160
然后把兔笼擦干净
and wipe down the rabbit hutch.

136
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,160
知道了 玛格丽特
On it. Margaret?

137
00:04:51,838 --> 00:04:53,300
画笔 冰沙 笼子
Paint, smoothies, hutch.

138
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:53,780
知道了
Got it.

139
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,340
不好意思 这位是谁
Excuse me. Who's this?

140
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:56,480
她是玛格丽特 我的助理
That's Margaret, my assistant.

141
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,320
我没法有小孩
I couldn't have children.

142
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:01,540
父母志愿者不应该是这样的
This is not how it works with parent volunteers.

143
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,200
你对于"志愿者"的态度已经很随便了
You're already playing fast and loose

144
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:06,180
所以你想怎么样
with that term "volunteer," so...what do you say?

145
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:08,780
虽然我们不喜欢用"不"这个字
As much as we don't like to use the word "No" --

146
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,920
而且 如果这些小崽子们敢乱来
And, by the way, if any of these little tykes start acting up,

147
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,460
她可是有一百种方法让他们安生下来
she's not afraid to get out the wooden spoon.

148
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:15,500
杰 我知道你怕怕
Jay, I know it's a little scary,

149
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:18,360
但你必须得让她走
but you're going to have to let her go.

150
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:19,580
我不想让她走
I don't want her to go.

151
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,860
玛格丽特 走吧 我来吸引他的注意力
Margaret, just go. I'll distract him.

152
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,660
回来
Come back.

153
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:26,440
玛格丽特 不要回头
Margaret, don't turn around.

154
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,760
好吧 各位
Okay, men.

155
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:32,780
都过来
Gather 'round.

156
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,260
教学时间
Teachable moment.

157
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:38,280
不要把社区服务当成一种要求
Don't think of community service as a requirement.

158
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:41,180
把清洁这座公园当成一个机会
Think of cleaning up this park as an opportunity.

159
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:42,420
得肝炎的机会吗
To get hepatitis?

160
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:44,400
让世界更美好的机会
To make the world a better place.

161
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:45,980
所以我才来的
That's why I'm here.

162
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:47,440
我已经做完我该做的时间了
I already did my required hours.

163
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,380
用这种方式表明你还是处男挺酷炫的
That's a fancy way of saying you're a virgin.

164
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:53,260
随便你们开玩笑 但这种经历在申请纽约大学
Joke all you want, but this looks good on an application to NYU

165
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:55,560
加州大学洛杉矶分校或肯德基时会很有用
or UCLA or KFC.

166
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:59,623
好吧 别说废话了 开始捡垃圾吧
Okay, stop trash-talking and start trash picking...up.

167
00:05:59,695 --> 00:06:00,909
我一会儿就来
I-I'll get that.

168
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,240
是你啊
There he is.

169
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:04,680
你好啊
You.

170
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:07,040
有多久没见了 房地产先生
How long's it been, Mr. Real estate?

171
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,300
你说呢 这位先生
Well, you tell me, Mr. You.

172
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,920
我通常很擅长记名字和脸
I'm usually really good with names and faces,

173
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,640
可我不记得这个人是谁了
but I could not remember who this guy was.

174
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:18,000
幸好 我知道一个好问题
Fortunately, I found that one perfectly worded question

175
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,460
能让你知道想要的所有信息
can get you all the information you need.

176
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:22,220
一切都好吗
How's things?

177
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:22,820
很好
Good.

178
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,340
你美丽的妻子近来如何
How's the beautiful wife?

179
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:27,140
克莱尔过得很好
Claire's great. Yeah.

180
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:28,620
多谢你的问候
Thank you so much for asking.

181
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:31,702
那 那你怎么样啊
How's... how's your situation?

182
00:06:31,702 --> 00:06:33,459
你知道的 老样子
You know, same old, same old.

183
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:35,600
实际上 这个时候遇到你我很高兴
Actually, I'm glad I'm running into you like this.

184
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:37,100
我的车刚被拖走了
My car just got towed,

185
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,269
我的钱包和手机都在里面
and my wallet and cellphone were in there.

186
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,820
你能借我点钱打的吗
Could you possibly lend me some money for cab fare or...

187
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:44,060
好
Yes.

188
00:06:44,143 --> 00:06:45,521
-多谢 -没事
- Thanks. - Of course.

189
00:06:45,532 --> 00:06:47,860
给你四十块外加一点零钱
How's, uh, $40 with a little extra

190
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:48,980
以防万一 如何
in case you run into trouble?

191
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:52,180
我希望你能来得及赶回家
I want to make sure you get back to your house in, uh --

192
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,260
希望赶得上吃晚饭
Time for dinner, I hope.

193
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,100
多谢了 哥们儿 你最棒了
Thanks, man. You're the best.

194
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:56,720
老爸
Hey, Dad.

195
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,400
天哪
Oh, my god.

196
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:01,040
我上次见你的时候 你才这么点大
Last time I saw you, you were so small.

197
00:07:01,501 --> 00:07:03,200
我得走了 多谢 朋友
I better run. Thanks, pal.

198
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,060
是啊 伙计 见到你真好
All right, buddy. Good to see you.

199
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:06,340
老爸
Dad.

200
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,100
那个人刚把你骗了
That guy just scammed you.

201
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,300
不 他没有
No, he didn't.

202
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:10,660
这是经典的诈骗方式
It's a classic scam.

203
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:12,780
假装认识对方然后借钱
You pretend you know someone and then borrow money.

204
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:13,680
好吧
Okay.

205
00:07:13,945 --> 00:07:17,745
大家围过来 教学时刻
Men, gather 'round. Teachable mome-- hey.

206
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,460
围成一个圈 过来的意思是围成圈
Just -- a circle. Gather means a circle.

207
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,140
你们刚刚看到了什么
What did you just see?

208
00:07:23,248 --> 00:07:24,720
小松鼠在吃创可贴
A squirrel eating a band-aid.

209
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:28,000
不 你们看到了一个人对朋友伸出援手
No. You saw a man helping out a friend in need.

210
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,500
如果他是你朋友 那他叫什么
If he was your friend, what's his name?

211
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:31,720
只是突然想不起来了
That slipped my mind.

212
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,040
你认得他的样子吗
Did you recognize him at all?

213
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:35,020
先生们 不要像卢克把别人都看扁
Gentlemen, don't be cynics like Luke.

214
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:37,340
不要让你们的紧身牛仔裤限制了良心供血
Don't let your skinny jeans cut off the blood to your hearts.

215
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:38,560
我支持你 菲尔
I'm with you, Phil.

216
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,540
我相信人性本善
I choose to believe in the goodness of men.

217
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,220
你鞋子上沾着一个套套
You have a condom stuck to your shoe.

218
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:48,100
被告对14号陪审员所言无异议
Defense also has no objection to juror 14.

219
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,160
继续 15号陪审员
Moving on, juror 15.

220
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,900
来吧 随便问 我是美国人
Here. Ask me anything. I am an American.

221
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,280
好吧
All right.

222
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,240
如果有人请了律师
When someone hires a lawyer,

223
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:58,140
你觉得他们更可能有罪吗
do you think they're more likely to be guilty?

224
00:07:58,660 --> 00:07:59,100
不
No.

225
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:00,180
谢谢
Thank you.

226
00:08:00,761 --> 00:08:02,560
如果他们像他那样玩头发
When they play with their hair like he is,

227
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,580
那我就知道他们有罪了
that's when I know that they're guilty.

228
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,920
法官大人 我们请求免职15号陪审员
Your honor, we request dismissal of juror 15.

229
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,000
为什么 我很擅长解读人性
Why? I'm very good at reading people.

230
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:10,760
他有罪
He is guilty.

231
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,320
另外 他后面那个男人也是
And, by the way, so is the guy that is behind him.

232
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,560
他都没有受审
He's not even on trial.

233
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:16,840
那他应该受审
Well, then he should be.

234
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,900
我不知道你做了什么 但你肯定做了
I don't know what you did, but you did it!

235
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,560
法官大人
Your honor.

236
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,640
他溜了
He's getting away.

237
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,600
15号陪审员 你被免职了
Juror 15, you are dismissed.

238
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,520
不 求你了 法官阁下
Ay! No, please, your excellency.

239
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:28,220
我只是想履行公民义务
I just want to do my part as a citizen.

240
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,800
女士 请不要犯傻了 出去
Lady, you can stop acting crazy. You got out.

241
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,860
姑娘们 这边 请进
Ladies, right this way. Come on in.

242
00:08:37,940 --> 00:08:39,120
你在外公的办公室里工作吗
Oh, you're in grandpa's office?

243
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,820
当然了
Yeah. Of course I am.

244
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:42,260
这没什么 我一直在这里
It's no big deal. I'm in here all the time.

245
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:45,700
基本上 每天的这个时间都在
I mean, practically every day at this...this point.

246
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,900
这个
This is...

247
00:08:47,168 --> 00:08:49,610
这椅子平常不是这样的
It's not usually such a...thing.

248
00:08:49,610 --> 00:08:50,840
好了 你们坐吧
There we go. Have a seat.

249
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,100
身上有纹身的那个人还在装卸货车间工作吗
Does that guy with the tattoos still work on the loading docks?

250
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:54,560
我十五岁的时候 我第一次被人嘘就是他
When I was 15, he gave me my first catcall.

251
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,740
那天应该是他最后一天上班
Pretty sure that was his last day.

252
00:08:58,400 --> 00:08:59,060
杰呢
where's Jay?

253
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,980
他不在 今天我代班
He's not here, but I'm filling in.

254
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,100
有事吗
What can I do you for?

255
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:03,380
我明天再来
I'll ask him tomorrow.

256
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:04,460
你确定
Are you sure?

257
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,840
男人总是被强势的女人吓到
Men are often intimidated by a strong, powerful woman.

258
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,040
杰在吗
Jay around?

259
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,020
他不在
No, he's not.

260
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:12,880
糟了
Oh, damn it.

261
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,180
可是掌控大局的人还在
Captain's chair is not empty.

262
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:18,040
让我来帮你吧
I'm here. Let me help you.

263
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,060
-你确定 -确定
- Seriously? - Seriously, huh?

264
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:23,980
我们要送100个装了镜子的门
Okay. Well, we need to take a delivery of 100 mirrored doors,

265
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:25,680
可是一号二号仓库都满了
but warehouse one and two are both full.

266
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,120
我知道怎么办 我能行
Okay, I know what to do. I've got this. Uh...

267
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:31,520
如果我们把抽屉全部塞到四号装卸车间
What if we move the drawers into that busted semi

268
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,480
那个烂半挂车里呢
in loading dock four?

269
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,840
-那样可以 因为 -二号仓库就空出来了
- And that works because-- - That frees up warehouse two.

270
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,820
最坏无非我们要晚一天才送到
Worst-case scenario, we're a day late on delivery.

271
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:37,580
客户会生气了
But they'll be mad at us.

272
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:38,800
如果我们在运费上折中一下呢
We'll give them a break off shipping?

273
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:39,820
我不知道 也许
I don't know. Maybe like --

274
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:41,160
打九折
10%! Ha.

275
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,880
成功了
We did it. Yeah!

276
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:46,280
干得漂亮 大伙
Good job, team.

277
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,340
我在这里的工作就是
You see, what I did there

278
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:50,900
构建一个解决问题的整体框架
is I created a framework for problem solving,

279
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,179
但是我不会直接告诉他们答案
and I didn't spoon-feed them the answers.

280
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:54,700
这就是绝妙的管理技能
It's just good management.

281
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:57,560
-是啊 -太绝妙了
- Yeah. - That's exactly what it looked like.

282
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:01,100
杰 我需要你帮忙决定 不好
Hey, Jay, I need a decision on that -- oh, boy.

283
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,140
回来 多姆
Get back here, Dom.

284
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,940
要决定什么
What needs to be decided?

285
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:07,940
赫姆要退休了 我们要为他举办派对
Well, we're throwing that party later for Herm's retirement,

286
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,920
杰特别擅长
and Jay's just sort of the master

287
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,200
给别人选蛋糕
when it comes to picking out cakes.

288
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,260
我来吧 我来选蛋糕
Oh, I'm here. I can pick out a cake.

289
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:14,640
冰淇淋蛋糕
Ice cream cake.

290
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:16,440
我说不好
I don't know about that.

291
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,640
就是个蛋糕而已 就它了
It's a cake. It'll be fine.

292
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,480
-有什么方式能让我联系 -赶紧去买吧
- Okay, is there a number where I could reach... - Just get it.

293
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,000
到杰吗
Jay?

294
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:23,140
不管事大事小
No matter how big or small the issue,

295
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,160
下属希望他们的领导有决断力
people want their leaders to be decisive.

296
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,180
-绝对的 -当然
- Oh, definitely. - Of course.

297
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:29,320
-什么口味 -薄荷味
- What flavor? - Mint chip.

298
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,320
-还是算了 -我说了薄荷味
- I'll come back. - I said mint chip!

299
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:35,560
乔 你想...
Hey, Joe! You want to...

300
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,420
我看起来像《灵异第六感》里的布鲁斯·威利斯
I'm like Bruce Willis in "The Sixth Sense."

301
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:39,800
杰 你能把手工桌
Jay, will you please put the craft table

302
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:40,840
放到麻毯上吗
over on the hemp rug?

303
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:42,460
不
No.

304
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:45,000
你说不爱用"不"这个字 可我咋老听见你用
For a word you don't use, I'm sure hearing it a lot.

305
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,060
那个才是手工桌
That's the craft table.

306
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:47,480
你现在拿的是情感桌
You're holding the feelings table,

307
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,300
我们只在谈论各自感受的时候才用
where we talk about how we feel.

308
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:53,820
桌子先生 我真想把你摔在她身上
Hey, Mr.Table, I feel like breaking you over a hippie.

309
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:55,840
你可是律师
Well, you're the lawyer.

310
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:58,040
我什么时候才能再去陪审团啊
When can I go to jury duty again?

311
00:10:58,260 --> 00:10:59,420
我也不知道
you know, I have no idea.

312
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,940
你算是第一个问这种问题的人
You're literally the first person who has ever asked that.

313
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:03,340
我太难过了
I am so frustrated.

314
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:06,000
这让我想起小时候还在村子里
This reminds me when I was a little girl in my village

315
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,260
当时我们一点权力[电力]都没有
and we had no power.

316
00:11:07,272 --> 00:11:08,980
你是说村里的电视
Oh, this is the story about the TV set

317
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,080
全靠驴子发电那个故事吗
powered by the donkey, right?

318
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:12,040
不是 我说的是政治权力
No, political power.

319
00:11:12,050 --> 00:11:14,187
我们没有任何发言权
We had no say in anything.

320
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,860
可现在我是美国人了
But now I am an American,

321
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:18,160
我以为事情会不一样
so I thought things were going to be different.

322
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:20,960
我想要听证词 看证据
I wanted to listen to testimony, look at the evidence,

323
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:24,780
看到有人带着新的信息闯进来
have somebody burst in with new information.

324
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:27,480
米奇尔 猜猜发生了什么
Mitchell, guess what just happened.

325
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,220
你早回家了
You're home early.

326
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:30,279
我周一周三周五都有两小时的午休
I have a two-hour lunch Monday, Wednesday, and Friday.

327
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:31,500
夏天也不用工作
And summers off.

328
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,200
我要开始拿低薪了
I'm beginning to get the low pay.

329
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,180
这是刚刚发来的
This just in.

330
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:38,720
胡娇说 如果杰马库斯和雷蒙德都来 他就不来了
Pepper says he's not coming if both J'marcus and Raymond are here.

331
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:41,180
我要是想在这么小的地方经受这么大的压力
"If I wanted this much tension in a space that small,

332
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,500
我还不如去我妈那里
I'd go up to my mother's room."

333
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:43,580
这太刻薄了
That's not nice.

334
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,940
我们不能再来一个糟糕的派对了
We can't afford to have another bad party.

335
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:49,220
你现在就得打给雷蒙德取消邀请
You have to call Raymond right now and un-invite him.

336
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,280
我不敢相信你和胡娇
I-I can't believe you and Pepper

337
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,920
居然对人毫无同情心
aren't being more compassionate about this.

338
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,120
雷蒙德也是人啊
Raymond is a human being.

339
00:11:53,130 --> 00:11:56,500
为什么不能邀请玛吉库斯和罗兰德他们俩
What is the problem with inviting Majarcus and Roland?

340
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:57,820
他们分手了
They had a horrible breakup.

341
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:58,860
就在几个月前
Months ago.

342
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,520
歌洛莉亚 你说呢
Gloria, what do you think?

343
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:03,740
在作出判决之前 我需要更多信息
I think I need to know more before I adjudicate.

344
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:04,740
判决
Adjudicate?

345
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:08,220
在天空晴朗 驴子还有劲的时候
When the skies were clear and the donkey was very strong,

346
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:10,277
我们会看《洛杉矶法律》
we would watch "L.A. Law".

347
00:12:12,013 --> 00:12:14,638
那是模型屋
That is the mockup room.

348
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:15,840
大伙好啊
Hey, guys.

349
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:17,460
继续做模型[嘲笑]
Keep up the mocking.

350
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,040
保持幽默总是有必要的
It's important to keep it fun.

351
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:23,780
看看 设计团队正在开会
Look at that. The design team's having a meeting.

352
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:25,180
你说我们要不要进去
What do you say we go in there

353
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,165
说几句"干得好"之类的
and give them a couple "Attaboys", huh?

354
00:12:27,165 --> 00:12:29,160
不了 他们看上去很忙
No. No, they look really busy.

355
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:29,940
别说笑了
Don't be silly.

356
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:32,254
每个人都想跟老板面对面接触
Everybody wants face time with the boss.

357
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,340
老妈 你还好吗
Mom, are you okay?

358
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,540
艾丽克斯 我没事
Alex, I'm fine.

359
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:39,800
-我的天 -怎么了
- Oh, my God. - What?

360
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,820
你的瞳孔就跟五分硬币一样大
Your pupil is the size of a nickel.

361
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:44,040
感觉像是半个你正在咆哮
It looks like half of you went to a rave.

362
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:46,480
克莱尔 我们有个库存问题
Claire, we have a storage problem.

363
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:48,640
如果是带镜子的门的事 我应该已经解决了
If it's those mirrored doors, I think I solved that one.

364
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,138
不是 有个白痴给赫姆订了一个冰淇淋蛋糕
No, some idiot ordered Herm an ice cream cake.

365
00:12:51,138 --> 00:12:52,520
你们这么叫人白痴不好
I don't think that name-calling--

366
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,960
等等 这跟库存有什么关系
wait, how is that a storage problem?

367
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:56,520
冰箱里根本放不下那玩意儿
The damn thing won't fit in the freezer.

368
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:57,980
融化得跟什么似的
It's melting like a son of a bitch.

369
00:12:58,100 --> 00:13:01,240
行 那就找一间最小的房间
Well, then, um, find the smallest room we've got

370
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:04,009
把冷气开到最大
and crank the A/C full blast, hmm?

371
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:05,220
-好建议 -谢谢你
- That's a great idea. - Thank you.

372
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,460
或许我们还能把杂物间的温度调高点
Maybe later, we could turn the heat up in the broom closet,

373
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,320
好烤些玛芬蛋糕吃
bake muffins.

374
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,620
完全悲剧
Complete disaster.

375
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:11,100
我有话要说
I'm gonna say something.

376
00:13:11,181 --> 00:13:13,380
你们这么说也太荒唐了吧
You people are being ridiculous.

377
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,740
不就是个该死的薄荷蛋糕吗
It's a freaking mint chip cake.

378
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:15,520
薄荷味的吗
Mint chip?

379
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,740
是的 薄荷味
Yeah, mint chip.

380
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:17,920
你们会喜欢的
You're gonna love it.

381
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,660
就算它融了一点 那又如何
And if it's melting, so what?

382
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:20,900
我们把派对提前就是了
We move the party up a little.

383
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,540
干脆 你们叫所有人
In fact, why don't you tell everybody

384
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,060
在十分钟内布置好一切
to be in the mill in 10 minutes.

385
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:25,080
但是杰赶不过来
But Jay's not here.

386
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,870
对呀 谁来给赫姆致告别词呢
Yeah, who will give Herm's farewell speech?

387
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:27,380
我啊
I will.

388
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:30,869
我会给他一个此生最棒的告别词
Give him the best farewell speech Herm has ever heard.

389
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:34,440
老妈 你确定你要上吗
Mom, are you sure you're up for this?

390
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,720
就是 你看起来晕乎乎的
Yeah, you look a little loopy.

391
00:13:36,060 --> 00:13:37,860
你们别担心 我能搞定
You know what? I'll be fine.

392
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:41,420
不过我首先得搞清楚赫姆是哪一位
Just as soon as I figure out who Herm is.

393
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:44,340
继续坚持 各位男士
Keep it up, gentlemen.

394
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:47,360
老爸 你还记得那次你被人敲竹杠吗
Hey, dad, remember that time you were getting ripped off?

395
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:48,220
你怎么还念念不忘
You're still on this.

396
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,020
我拍了一张那人的照片发给老妈了
I took a picture of the guy and sent it to mom.

397
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:52,480
她发誓说从没见过那个人
She swears she's never seen him before in her life.

398
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:53,400
对于她在酒吧遇到过的所有人
Your mom could say that

399
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,720
你妈都能说她不认识
about anyone she met at a party with an open bar.

400
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:58,540
有人又需要受点人生教育啦
Sounds like someone could use another teachable moment.

401
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:00,022
-不用了 老爸 -大家快过来抱团
- I'm good, Dad. - Men, gather 'round.

402
00:14:00,022 --> 00:14:02,106
人生教 我了个
Teachable mo-- mother of...

403
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,080
卢克还是固执地认为我被骗了
Luke here still thinks I got ripped off,

404
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,500
但是如果那人真是骗子
but if that guy wasn't legit,

405
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:08,280
他又怎么知道卢克是我儿子呢
how did he know that Luke was my son?

406
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,540
因为我管你叫老爸
Because I called you Dad.

407
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:11,320
但是他怎么知道你以前很小呢
But how did he know that you used to be small?

408
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,500
我发现这里有点问题了
I get the problem with that one.

409
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:15,280
菲尔 别被他的嘲讽扰乱自己
Phil, don't give in to his hipster cynicism.

410
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,000
我很敬佩你这么天真地信任别人
I admire your childlike faith in people.

411
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:19,480
还有卢克 你回答我这个问题
And, Luke, answer me this.

412
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,660
如果这人真是个骗子
If this guy is such a con man,

413
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,560
他又是怎么知道你爸是"房地产先生"的
how did he know your dad was Mr. Real Estate?

414
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:24,420
棒呆
Boom!

415
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:26,720
快来人拿个麦克风给这孩子扔扔
Someone give this kid a mic to drop.

416
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:28,540
你还真问住我了
You got me.

417
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:31,160
我现在脑子都还晕乎乎的
I'm actually feeling a little dizzy because of that.

418
00:14:31,402 --> 00:14:33,440
我的整个三观都被震撼了
My whole world view has been rocked.

419
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:35,520
在晕倒之前 我得赶紧坐下
I'm just gonna sit down before I pass out.

420
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,580
坐在鸽子粪上还装得这么拽
Pretty smug for a guy sitting on pigeon droppings.

421
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,800
那我也值了
Totally worth it.

422
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:50,920
当时我站在门外觉得很难过
I was standing outside feeling sorry for myself.

423
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,200
*孤单小豹拉里*
*Larry the lonely leopard*

424
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,640
*身上斑点去不掉*
*Couldn't change his spots*

425
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:58,840
*但是只要真心微笑*
*But once he put his smile on*

426
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:01,780
*好朋友们全围绕*
*Look at all the friends he's got*

427
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:04,140
然后我意识到自己就是那只孤单小豹拉里
Then I realized I was Larry the lonely leopard.

428
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,540
我只需要重露笑容就好了
I just needed to put my smile on.

429
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,400
那首歌真是穿透灵魂
That song works on so many levels.

430
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:12,420
大家好 我是乔的爸爸
Hi, gang. I'm Joe's Dad.

431
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:14,460
有谁想听故事吗
Anybody want to hear a story?

432
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:17,680
-这是个好提议 杰 -那好
- That's a great idea, Jay! - Okay.

433
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:20,560
这个故事叫《小小小屋子》
This one's called "The teeny tiny house".

434
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,640
在一座很小很小的镇上
"In a teeny tiny town...

435
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,400
一个很小很小的街区里
"On a teeny tiny block,"

436
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:29,380
有一座很小很小的房子 里面有
"Stood a teeny tiny house with a teeny tiny --"

437
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:30,380
你好老
You're old.

438
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:32,100
你见过我妻子吗 大耳仔
You seen my wife, Big Ears?

439
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,560
那之后 大耳仔的家长和我
After that, Big Ears' parents and I

440
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,740
不得不在情感桌上坐下来谈话
had to spend a little time at the feelings table.

441
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:40,560
我看看是不是搞清楚这事了
Let me see if I'm understanding this.

442
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:42,980
总的说来 你们认识雷达的时间久些
So, you have known Radar longer,

443
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:45,500
但杰玛玛为人更风趣
but Jemima is the fun one.

444
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,860
是的 为你越来越接近人家真正的名字点个赞
Yes, and kudos for really zeroing in on those names.

445
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:50,440
拜托 雷蒙更有趣一点好吗
Come on. Raymond's fun.

446
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:51,700
说一件他有趣的事来听听
Name one fun thing he does.

447
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,340
还一件 太多件了好吗
One -- so many things.

448
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:55,640
好吧 听着 他干过这事
Okay, this, he does this thing

449
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:57,640
模仿他父母的答录机
where he imitates his parents' answering machine.

450
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:00,320
真的超搞笑 每次模仿都搞笑死了
It's hilarious. It kills every time.

451
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,160
-那是杰马库斯好吗 -呵呵了
- And it's J'marcus. - Damn it.

452
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:05,640
米奇尔 为什么这个雷蒙德对你来说这么重要
Mitchell, why is this Raymond so important to you?

453
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,420
到底有什么事是不能告诉我们的
What is it that you're not telling us?

454
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,220
没什么
Nothing.

455
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:11,000
难道你不是对他动心了吗
Isn't it true that you have feelings for him?

456
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,580
我没有
No.

457
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,680
承认吧 你就是喜欢他
Admit it. You have a crush on him.

458
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:14,340
我没有
I don't.

459
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:16,760
你爱他 你想和他在一起
You love him. You want to be with him.

460
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:20,300
而且除非卡梅隆退出了 你才会死心
And you won't stop until Cameron is out of the picture.

461
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:21,753
好了 好了 你疯了
Okay, okay, you're -- you're crazy.

462
00:16:21,753 --> 00:16:22,952
-那到底为什么 -因为
- Then why? - Be--

463
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:25,180
因为我就是雷蒙德
Because I am Raymond.

464
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:26,720
什么
What?

465
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,032
是的 如果我们分手了
Yeah, if -- if we ever broke up,

466
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:30,380
我们所有的朋友都会站在你那边
all of our friends would pick you,

467
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:31,680
我会被抛弃的
and I'd be the one who's left behind.

468
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:33,360
亲爱的 不是这样的
Honey, that's not true.

469
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,940
我会逼他们请你参加各种圈内活动的
I would make them invite you to stuff.

470
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:38,820
他在说谎 看他玩自己头发就知道
He's lying. I can tell from the way he's playing with his hair.

471
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,589
不 我觉得他说的是真的
No, I-I think you really got to it.

472
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,100
-快坦白 -好吧 是小卡
- Say it. Okay, fine. Cam!

473
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:44,140
是小卡好了吧 我担心的是小卡
Cam's the one, all right? Cam's the one I'm worried about.

474
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:45,560
他才是那个会被抛弃的人
He's the one who's gonna be left behind.

475
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:46,940
我的追问结束了
I rest my case.

476
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:48,960
可是我还没问完
Well, I don't rest mine.

477
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:51,160
为什么你觉得我会被抛弃
Why do you think I'm the one that's gonna be left behind?

478
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,120
我可是"舞会女神"[备受瞩目]好吗
I'm the belle of the ball.

479
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:53,740
就是这样 这种话
Right there -- that's the type of thing

480
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:55,100
你应该让别人去说
you should let other people say.

481
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,500
而且还要你是女生
About a woman.

482
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,540
没人会听你的政治呼声
Nobody really cares about your political rants.

483
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:00,520
朋友们才不想听科赫兄弟[两个富老头]的事呢
Our friends don't want to hear about the Koch Brothers.

484
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,240
除非你说的是一群帅基佬
Unless you're talking about a couple of hot guys

485
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,460
在夜店里的卫生间共浴
in a bathroom at a nightclub.

486
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:04,720
小卡 你还真是口无遮拦
Cam, you have no filter.

487
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:06,320
不管想到什么粗俗的事情你都照样说出来
You say whatever rude thing you're thinking,

488
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:07,460
这样会把别人惹不高兴[费泽斯]
and that ruffles feathers.

489
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,080
费泽斯有严重的口臭
Feathers has terrible breath,

490
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:11,900
而我是唯一一个坦诚告诉他的人
and I was the only one with the decency to tell him.

491
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:13,960
好 行了 你们俩都给我坐下
Okay, that's it. Both of you sit down.

492
00:17:14,140 --> 00:17:15,360
我做好决定了
I have reached my decision.

493
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,240
雷蒙德可以来参加派对
Raymond is coming to the party.

494
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,700
这会是个明智的先例
It's a smart precedent to set,

495
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:21,700
因为据我今天听到的
because after what I heard here today,

496
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:23,340
我觉得你们两个
I think there is a big chance

497
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:25,740
以后很有可能都会被大家遗弃
that both of you are going to be left out.

498
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,260
你又没宣誓 非得要说真话吗
You know you're not under oath, right?

499
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,480
这不是他嘛
There he is.

500
00:17:33,704 --> 00:17:35,807
好久没见了 运动服先生
How long's it been, Mr. Sport Coat?

501
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:40,360
终极的教育时刻到来了
And there it was. The ultimate teachable moment.

502
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,680
我猜答案是什么也没有
I guess the answer is nothing.

503
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:46,400
没什么能让我们跟动物有所区别
Nothing separates us from animals.

504
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,880
成熟点吧 曼尼 人类基本都很糟
Grow up, Manny. Human beings are basically terrible.

505
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:51,660
你们搞什么鬼
What the hell?

506
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:54,380
他来了 满口废话先生
There he is! Mr. Full-of-Garbage.

507
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,440
你们在干什么
What are you doing?

508
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:58,460
报仇 你利用我的善良 假装认识我
Payback for turning a bunch of innocent kids into cynics

509
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:01,120
就是你这种人让孩子们不再相信他人
by preying on my good nature and pretending you know me!

510
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,900
菲尔 我是蒙蒂·雷蒙医生
Phil -- Dr. Monty Lemon.

511
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:05,660
是我接生卢克的
I delivered Luke.

512
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:08,360
蒙蒂·雷蒙医生比你瘦 头发比你多
Dr. Monty Lemon was thinner, had more hair,

513
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:10,720
而且他比你年轻十五岁
and was a good 15 years younger than you -- oh.

514
00:18:11,606 --> 00:18:14,611
对哦 我婴儿时的照片上有你
Yeah. You're in my baby photos.

515
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:20,160
谁想要蛋糕 拿杯子过来
Anybody wants cake, grab a cup.

516
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,120
给我来点
I'll have some.

517
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,160
是薄荷味的
It's mint chip.

518
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:29,200
成了
Did it.

519
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:32,140
拿到了赫姆的个人档案 还写了超赞的演讲稿
I got Herm's personnel file, and I wrote a kickass speech.

520
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,860
你的眼睛变成蓝黑色了
Your eye is turning black and blue.

521
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:36,219
还有你的手是怎么了
Yeah, and -- and what happened to your hand?

522
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:36,680
没什么
Nothing.

523
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:39,020
我打开档案柜的时候划破了手指
I just gashed it trying to get into the filing cabinet.

524
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,760
只不过缝了一两针 没什么大不了的
Nothing a stitch or two at urgent care can't fix.

525
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:44,640
"老板" 我们真要这样做吗
"Boss", are we gonna do this?

526
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,220
是的
Oh, we're doing this.

527
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:48,300
我知道今天发生了很多事
I know it's been a tricky day,

528
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:51,120
但我很高兴你们俩能在此见证这一切
but I am so glad the two of you are here to see this.

529
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:53,700
好了 各位 请都过来
Okay, everyone, gather 'round.

530
00:18:54,588 --> 00:18:55,788
都过来
Just bring it in.

531
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,060
请大家把注意力都集中到我这
Let me get your attention here.

532
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,697
老妈 老妈
Mom! Mom!

533
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:02,320
可恶的冰淇淋蛋糕
Stupid ice cream cake.

534
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:04,340
我没事 天哪
I'm okay. Ooh. Oh, God.

535
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:05,460
妈妈 别动
Mom, stay down.

536
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,380
不 我得起来
No. I need this.

537
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:10,060
我知道你觉得要给我们留下好印象 但真的不用
I know you think you need to impress us, but you don't.

538
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:12,240
从小到大 你一直都感动着我们
You've impressed us our whole lives.

539
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:13,400
尤其是今天
And especially today.

540
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:16,020
除了你 没人能忍受这种惩罚
Nobody but you could put up with this much punishment

541
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:16,680
还继续装下去的
and keep going.

542
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:17,700
这对我意义重大
It means so much.

543
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:21,100
真的 但我还有工作要做
It really does, but I've got a job to do.

544
00:19:21,596 --> 00:19:22,867
我要做完它
And I'm gonna do it.

545
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:35,520
赫姆对很多人来说意义非凡
Herm is so many things to so many people.

546
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:38,760
在他三个儿子心里 他是榜样
To his three sons, he is a role model.

547
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:42,860
对他妻子德洛丽丝来说 他是个忠诚的丈夫
To his wife, Dolores, he is a devoted husband.

548
00:19:42,998 --> 00:19:46,160
对于他的六只营救犬来说 他...
And to his six rescue beagles, he...

549
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,780
-弄错赫姆了 -什么
- Wrong Herm. - What?

550
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:50,060
你说的是赫姆·安德森
You're talking about Herm Anderson.

551
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:53,240
今天退休的人是赫姆·科沃斯基
Herm Kowalski is the one who's retiring today.

552
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,260
有两个叫赫姆的吗
There are two Herms?

553
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:56,880
-有三个 -好吧 我放弃
- Three. - Okay, I'm out.

554
00:19:59,351 --> 00:20:00,921
杰
Jay?

555
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,640
在这喝酒呢
In here with the booze.

556
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,280
你怎么样
How are you?

557
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:06,700
挺好的 怎么了
Fine. Why?

558
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,080
学校来电话了
The school called,

559
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:11,220
他们说有个坏孩子取笑了你
and they said that a mean boy made fun of you.

560
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,440
他可能会听到我们的谈话
He can probably hear us from here.

561
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:15,160
那孩子的耳朵比斯黛拉的还大
Kid had ears bigger than Stella's.

562
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,920
除了这些呢 感觉如何
Other than that, how was it?

563
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:19,100
就像我玩那个滑滑管一样 不合适
Like me in the tube slide -- not a good fit.

564
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:20,740
这事不适合我
Just not my thing.

565
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:22,860
别再跟我说那些增进感情的说辞了
And don't give me that business about bonding,

566
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:24,620
因为乔根本不知道我在那
because Joe didn't even know I was there.

567
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:26,160
不知是否能让你好受点
Well, if it makes you feel any better,

568
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,940
陪审员的事被拒绝了
I got rejected from jury duty,

569
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:29,980
所以你再也不用去学校了
so you don't have to go to school anymore.

570
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:31,110
妈妈 妈妈
Mommy! Mommy!

571
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:37,520
今天在学校怎么样
How was your school day?

572
00:20:37,592 --> 00:20:40,888
最棒的一天 因为爸爸去了
Best day ever 'cause Daddy was there.

573
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:41,440
真的吗
Really?

574
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,820
你喜欢爸爸陪你上学吗
Did you like Daddy being in school?

575
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,800
他做好吃的 还读了书
He made snacks, he read books,

576
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:49,680
而且现在我管汤米叫大耳朵
and now I call Tommy "Big Ears."

577
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:50,780
很高兴你喜欢
I'm glad that stuck.

578
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:53,040
太好了
That's so nice.

579
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,300
爸爸 你明天还去吗
Daddy, can you come back tomorrow?

580
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:58,180
你真的希望我明天还去吗
Do you really want me to come back tomorrow?

581
00:20:58,540 --> 00:20:59,060
是的
Yeah.

582
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:00,900
谁又能想到呢
What do you know?

583
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,860
我大受欢迎
I'm a hit.

584
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:08,480
有人吗
Anyone there?

585
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:10,880
帮个忙好吗
Little help?

586
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:13,240
谁
Hello?

587
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:14,180
汤米
Tommy?

588
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:15,280
汤米
Tommy.

589
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:17,440
我被卡在这里了
I'm kind of stuck here.

590
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,480
你能去找个大人来吗
Could you go get a grown-up?

591
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,260
抱歉 听不见你说话
Sorry. Can't hear you.

592
00:21:20,260 --> 00:21:20,680
真的吗
Really?

593
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:22,420
耳朵那么大都听不到吗
With those ears?

594
00:21:23,215 --> 00:21:24,780
对不起 我不该取笑你
I'm sorry, that was uncalled for.

595
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:25,080
你想要什么
What do you want?

596
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:26,200
钱吗 我有钱
Money? I got money.

597
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:28,880
拿去 信用卡随便刷
Go ahead, use the credit card.

598
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:30,390
你肯定没我老婆能花钱
You spend less than my wife.
